 # Existing JSON utility
 
-Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: weight. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+
+## Actions
+
+### weight
+Payload: `{"action":"weight","entries":[{"weight":n},...]}` — returns the total weight.
+
+### cache
+Weighted LRU action cache (capacity is total weight, not entry count). The cache starts empty for each payload.
+
+Payload: `{"action":"cache","capacity":<nonnegative integer>,"operations":[...]}`
+- `{"op":"put","key":<string>,"value":<JSON>,"weight":<positive integer>}` — stores the entry. Invalid capacity/weight raises ValueError. If `weight > capacity`, returns `{"stored":false,"evicted":[]}` and leaves the cache untouched (even when replacing an existing key). Otherwise the key becomes most-recently-used; after a replacement, the oldest OTHER entries are evicted (least-recently-used first) until total weight <= capacity. Returns `{"stored":true,"evicted":[keys in eviction order]}`.
+- `{"op":"get","key":<string>}` — hit returns `{"hit":true,"value":<stored value>}` and promotes the key to most-recently-used; miss returns `{"hit":false,"value":null}` without changing order.
+
+Returns `{"results":[one result per operation],"entries":[{key,value,weight}...]}` with entries in least-to-most recently used order. Empty operations return empty arrays.
